WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.800
- In 2020, Cardi B sued
YouTube vlogger Tasha K

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.470
for defamation, invasion of privacy

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.790
and intentional infliction
of emotional distress.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:09.320
Now, the verdict is in,

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.940
and Cardi B is looking like a
moneybag honey bag moneybag.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.150
Love it when we do these on singers.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:20.070
The jury ordered Tasha
K to pay $1.25 million

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.417
for defamation of character,

00:00:21.417 --> 00:00:24.040
$1.5 million in punitive damages

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.970
and $1.3 million to cover
Cardi B's legal fees.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.217
I guess when Cardi B said,

00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:32.030
"Spoil me in Prada, I'm
worth every dollar",

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.830
she apparently meant it.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.100
Now we've talked about defamation

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.260
many times on this channel,

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.740
specifically about how hard
it is for pubic figures

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.500
to win a defamation lawsuit.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.960
Well, credit to Cardi B and her lawyers,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.790
they successfully proved that
Tasha K made false claims

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:48.230
and did them with actual malice.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.863
If this verdict holds up,
Cardi B's gonna buy a palace.

00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:54.122
♪ Tasha K made claims with actual malice ♪

00:00:54.122 --> 00:00:57.373
♪ If this verdict holds up,
Cardi's gonna buy a palace ♪

00:00:57.373 --> 00:01:00.206
(cinematic music)

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.560
Hey Legal Eagles, it's time to think like,

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.970
like YouTube lawyer.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.550
That's kind of fun.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.050
So, just what is the beef
between Cardi B and Tasha K?

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.220
Is this the greatest legal fight

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:16.210
between someone who uses their
first name and last initial?

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.380
How did Cardi's lawyers convince a jury

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.650
that she had been defamed,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.420
and what did Tasha K argue in defense?

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.570
Well listen up, because you're
about to get a masterclass

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.210
in how Cardi B bossed
up and changed the game.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:29.660
Okay, so let's talk about the beef

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.990
between Cardi B and Tasha K.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.930
YouTuber Latasha Kebe,
also known as Tasha K,

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.810
is a popular podcast
host, vlogger and blogger.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.460
She posts interviews and opinion pieces

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.410
on her YouTube channel,
Unwind with Tasha K.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.210
She has over a million subscribers

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:47.440
and also hosts a streaming
service called tashaklive.com.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.480
Now, on September 19, 2018,
Tasha published a video

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.460
of an interview she conducted
with Starmarie Jones.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.750
Jones claimed that she had
been roommates with Cardi B

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.490
during Cardi's stripper days.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.210
Jones told Tasha that Cardi
had prostituted herself

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.460
to make a living before
she became a rap superstar.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.800
Jones said she lived with Cardi

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.310
and knew for a fact that Cardi got herpes.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.310
But as far back as 2018,

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.644
there was evidence that Starmarie Jones

00:02:11.644 --> 00:02:14.000
was not who she claimed to be.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.090
Before she went viral by claiming
to be Cardi's ex roommate,

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.530
Jones said that she
actually did not know Cardi

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.150
but felt jealousy over
Cardi's record deal.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.950
Later, she apparently concocted
a story about knowing Cardi.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.760
Tasha then repeated Jones' claims

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.610
on all of her social media channels.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.280
Should Tasha have believed
Starmarie's story?

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.170
Well, another YouTuber,
Empressive, says no.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.160
Empressive figured out that
Jones lied way back in 2018.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.140
In her video, she revealed
that Jones admitted

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.380
she had never met Cardi,

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.800
and points out that
Starmarie is very bitter

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.040
that her own music career never took off.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.840
Here, Empressive shows a clip
of Jones meeting with Tasha.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.340
Empressive says that she felt sorry

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.270
that Tasha fell for Jones' lies,

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.700
but she felt like it was
important to be responsible

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.610
about whose stories
vloggers choose to promote.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.010
Nevertheless, over the next three years,

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.900
Tasha again repeated the Jones claims

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.740
in at least 38 videos about Cardi B.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.240
She also discussed them during
Instagram Live recordings

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.440
and on Facebook.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.130
None of those videos portrayed
Cardi B in a positive light,

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.740
and of course, because of the
First Amendment, that's okay.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.970
In America, you can express
your own negative opinion

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:15.940
about someone else,

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.930
as long as you don't make up
false statements about them.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.730
You can even call them names.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.310
So did Tasha K cross the line

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:25.270
between defamation and opinion?

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.680
Well it depends on the details
of the actual statements,

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.700
but here's how the beef went down.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.350
Well first, on September 19, 2018,

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:32.910
Tasha published a video of herself

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.640
discussing the Jones' video.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.047
It was titled, "Exclusive:
Cardi B's Ex-Friend

00:03:37.047 --> 00:03:39.837
"Alleges Cardi B Kept A Huge
Box Filled with Monistat

00:03:39.837 --> 00:03:41.470
"and Reveals More."

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.580
The video got four million views.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.290
Cardi B's lawyers sent a cease
and desist letter to Tasha,

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.530
demanding immediate removal of the video.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.640
Tasha then doubled down on her claims,

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.097
publishing a video entitled,

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:54.627
"Actual Proof Cardi B
Knew Her Ex-Roommate,

00:03:54.627 --> 00:03:58.910
"Drake, Funky Dineva vs
Tamar, Beyonce Black Majic",

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.620
where she stated that everything said

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.250
in the September 19th video was true.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.300
This is an important shift in perspective.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.010
Originally, Tasha attributed
Jones as the source

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.790
for the assorted allegations
about Cardi's past,

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:11.980
and in terms of news reporting,

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.930
you often get more protection
in a defamation context

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:17.380
when you're simply reporting
what someone else has said,

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.210
compared to things that
you yourself have said.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:23.527
However, in the September
19th video, Tasha K said,

00:04:23.527 --> 00:04:27.380
"Everything that we said that
Jones said was accurate."

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.380
So did this set Tasha on a course

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:31.160
that she found hard to back down from?

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.920
Well, on December 18, 2018,

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.587
she published a video on YouTube entitled,

00:04:34.587 --> 00:04:37.367
"Tasha K Responds to
Cardi B's Defamation Suit

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:40.530
"and Offset's Dad calling
Cardi B Out, and More".

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.480
In this video, Tasha alleges
that when she was a stripper,

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.503
Cardi B used a beer bottle to,

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.690
well you can see what that says.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:52.680
Then on January 25, 2019,

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.430
Tasha tweeted that Cardi B had herpes.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.030
The tweet prompted Cardi to
formally request a retraction

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.920
and repudiation of these statements.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.300
Although Tasha temporarily
removed the videos and posts,

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.740
by September of 2021,

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.270
she had relisted and reposted the videos.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.870
In the meantime, Tasha
continued to repeat allegations

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.497
about prostitution and herpes in videos

00:05:10.497 --> 00:05:12.250
and Instagram Live sessions.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.030
On April 23, 2019,

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.967
Tasha published a video on YouTube called,

00:05:15.967 --> 00:05:20.077
"Tasha K Responds to Cardi
B's Mute Black Blogs Agenda,

00:05:20.077 --> 00:05:23.290
"Cardi Calls Shade Room
Owner a Water Buffalo".

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.310
I don't know what any
of these things mean.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:29.170
This is not my preferred
videos on YouTube,

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.830
but hopefully you can
parse what's going on here.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.268
In other videos and on
Instagram and Facebook posts,

00:05:34.268 --> 00:05:36.850
Tasha made these claims again and again,

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.850
just like she did with
the other allegations.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.620
She also claimed Cardi was a cheater

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.860
who had contracted the HPV virus.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.580
There's more, but by now,
you kinda get the point.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.087
Tasha K did not like Cardi B

00:05:46.087 --> 00:05:48.150
and was making lots of serious allegations

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.270
about Cardi's life as a stripper.

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:51.530
Now, I think it's important to point out

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.440
that yes, Cardi B was a stripper.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.960
She's given candid interviews
about that time in her life

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.080
and raps about it.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.180
However, being a stripper isn't
a get out of liability card

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:04.350
for Tasha K, which brings us
to the complaint at issue.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:08.040
On March 21, 2019, Cardi B sued
Tasha K and Starmarie Jones

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.070
in the US District Court

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:10.870
for the Northern District of Georgia.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.650
Although defamation
and invasion of privacy

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.230
are state law claims, the case
was filed in federal court

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.290
because the plaintiff and defendant

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.180
live in different states,

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.710
and the amount in
controversy was over $75,000.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.270
This is called diversity jurisdiction.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.500
Now, Jones chose not to
defend herself in the lawsuit,

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.000
so a New York Supreme Court judge

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.960
granted Cardi's motion
for default judgment.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:27.820
I'm not gonna go into why

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.680
this is in New York Court at the moment,

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.033
but as part of that judge's order,

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:33.650
the video was removed
and Jones was prohibited

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:35.240
from talking about the
defamatory statements

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.730
about Cardi in the future.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.360
The judge's order explicitly states

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.180
that as a matter of law,

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:42.420
the defendant's statements
that plaintiff had engaged

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.650
in prostitution and has or had herpes

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.340
are held to be defamatory,
as they are untrue

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.200
and were made without justification
or proof by defendant.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.570
Now the default judgment against Jones

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.590
put Tasha K in a precarious position.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:54.650
Cardi alleged that Tasha

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.500
made the following defamatory statements:

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.941
Cardi B was a prostitute,
Cardi B had certain STIs,

00:06:58.941 --> 00:07:01.370
Cardi B performed certain sexual acts,

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.770
and Cardi B took cocaine and ecstasy.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.440
Now, Tasha published these statements

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:06.490
on her social media sites,

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:08.500
garnering millions of views and likes.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.560
Cardi alleged that they
damaged her reputation

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.040
in the industry, with her fans,

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.280
and disrupted potential
business relationships.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.750
Now, Tasha K denied that
she had defamed Cardi.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.350
She alleged that all
the statements were true

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.550
and that they were not
made with actual malice.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:22.070
She argued that she had the right

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:24.820
to rely on Jones' original claims.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.770
Now, Cardi B's first and main
claim was for defamation.

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:29.250
We've covered defamation many times,

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.360
but you generally prove that
by showing four elements:

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:33.300
A false statement was
made about the plaintiff,

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.440
the statement was published

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.450
where other people saw or heard it,

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.630
the statement harmed the
plaintiff's reputation

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:41.380
and no privilege of defense
existed for the statement,

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:42.740
and Georgia law basically tracks

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.287
our basic understanding of defamation.

00:07:44.287 --> 00:07:46.550
And of course, you have to
have a certain mental state.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.230
Generally it's negligence

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.430
about the falsehood of the statements.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:51.620
But when you're dealing with
someone like a celebrity,

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:52.810
you have to have actual malice,

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.030
which means you knowingly

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:57.110
or recklessly said these false things.

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:58.040
That's the higher standard.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:58.900
It doesn't have anything to do

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:00.670
with actually not liking a person.

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.440
Actual malice is about knowingly

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:05.830
or recklessly repeating
these false statements.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.920
And of course, truth is
a defense to defamation.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.910
In other words, defamatory
statements must be false

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:11.040
to be actionable.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.710
You can say something mean about someone

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:13.590
that hurts their reputation,

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:17.490
as long as what you say is
accurate or it's opinion

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.900
or other things that don't rise
to the level of defamation.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.060
And here, there was no question

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.180
that the statements were published

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.710
and disseminated to third parties,

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.680
but the questions of whether
a particular communication

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:26.640
was defamatory

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:29.380
and whether the defendant had
the requisite mental state

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.470
were for the jury to decide.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:33.280
Now here, the mental state
is really interesting,

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.470
because usually, you only
have to prove negligence.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:38.440
But following in a famous
Supreme Court case,

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.450
New York Times vs Sullivan,

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:41.730
when you're dealing with a public figure,

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:43.740
you have to prove actual malice.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.440
In the Sullivan case,
the Supreme Court held

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.640
that public official
could not recover damages

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:48.910
for defamatory statements

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.720
regarding his or her official conduct,

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.021
unless it was proven that
the statement was made

00:08:52.021 --> 00:08:55.450
with actual malice, which
again, is a legal term

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.130
that has nothing to do
with hatred of a person.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:58.400
It's about the mental state

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:01.700
of knowing that the statements are false.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.940
Later, the Supreme Court
extended the actual malice rule

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.960
to apply to criticism of a public figure.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.507
Public figures are people who are,

00:09:07.507 --> 00:09:09.317
"intimately involved in the resolution

00:09:09.317 --> 00:09:11.585
"of important public questions
or, by reason of their fame,

00:09:11.585 --> 00:09:15.540
"shape events in areas of
concern to society at large."

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:16.830
Basically, the Supreme Court thought

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:19.120
that if it was too easy
to prove defamation,

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.190
then rich and influential people,

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.160
as well as government officials,

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.420
could use their power
to chill free speech.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.990
And that could certainly be a
concern in a case like this,

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:29.370
since an extremely famous person

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:31.632
who presumably has lots of money,

00:09:31.632 --> 00:09:35.490
sued someone who has
presumably fewer resources.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.530
And this is why Tasha K called out Cardi B

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:40.240
for attempting to silence
her voice as a vlogger.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.010
On the other hand, vloggers like Tasha K

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:45.210
have pretty big platforms
to spread malicious gossip,

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.630
and these days, everyone
has access to the Internet,

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.830
where these things can be repeated.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.830
So her success in social
media made her a bigger target

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.990
than someone who doesn't have
a big social media presence.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:58.070
Now, this wasn't necessarily an easy case.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:09:59.900
The judge in Cardi B's case concluded

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.260
that there was a genuine
dispute of material fact,

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.730
but whether all of Tasha
K's statements were,

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.640
in fact, false and defamatory,

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.630
and that it was going to be up to the jury

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:10.160
to decide these questions.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:11.320
For example, in this case,

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.740
Cardi denied ever being a
prostitute or using drugs.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:16.250
However, Tasha K offered
evidence that during interviews,

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.800
Cardi had talked about
engaging in sexual acts

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:19.930
in exchange for money.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:23.200
In that same video, Cardi B
discusses her use of drugs

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.960
and about having to pop pills
sometimes when necessary.

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.500
What does it mean to pop pills?

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.610
Does this imply that she
popped cocaine and Molly,

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:33.820
or that she took Benadryl and Tylenol?

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.070
The jury's job was to
review all the evidence

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:38.500
and decide whether these
statements were false.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.320
So let's talk about the
evidence regarding STIs.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.320
Juries who hear civil cases
review quite a lot of evidence,

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.070
and here's a list of the
exhibits admitted to the court

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.450
in this particular case.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:51.600
There are 1021 exhibits.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.740
Now the jury didn't
hear hours of testimony

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:54.770
on each of these exhibits,

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.720
but they did have access
to all this material,

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:59.890
which Cardi B alleged proved
the elements of her claims.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:01.930
And here's Tasha K's list of exhibits.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:04.371
She offered 125 exhibits
in an attempt to prove

00:11:04.371 --> 00:11:07.600
that what she said was true about Cardi B.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.040
And although we aren't privy
to the jury's deliberations,

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.330
we do know that Tasha failed to prove

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:15.350
that her comment about Cardi
B having STIs was true.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.260
In discovery, Tasha asked for an order

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.860
requiring Cardi to turn
over her medical records.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:21.900
Cardi had already submitted STI tests,

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.400
but did not fight the order.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:25.470
The judge granted her
request to produce material

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:26.480
under a protective order.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:28.910
That means that the judge
can see the medical records,

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.700
but that they are sealed from public view.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:32.470
And when you're talking
about medical records,

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:33.920
that makes perfect sense.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:37.190
And in December, the judge
reviewed Cardi's medical records

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:41.000
and ruled that they did not
show that Cardi had any STIs.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.277
Quote, "The Court has received
and reviewed the records

00:11:43.277 --> 00:11:45.407
"and finds that they are
not helpful to Defendant.

00:11:45.407 --> 00:11:48.217
"Accordingly, the Court will
file the records under seal.

00:11:48.217 --> 00:11:49.437
"At Plaintiff's request only,

00:11:49.437 --> 00:11:51.818
"the Court will release
the records to both sides

00:11:51.818 --> 00:11:53.367
"to be used at trial.

00:11:53.367 --> 00:11:55.537
"Otherwise, the records
shall not be opened

00:11:55.537 --> 00:11:57.617
"except with permission
of the District Judge

00:11:57.617 --> 00:11:59.110
"or the Court of Appeals."

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.490
And then there's evidence
about lying under oath.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:04.260
Why didn't Tasha K have more
credibility with the jury?

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:06.497
Well, she was caught lying on the stand.

00:12:06.497 --> 00:12:08.113
"On cross examination, Tasha K was asked,

00:12:08.113 --> 00:12:10.087
"'isn't it a fact that you
testified in your deposition

00:12:10.087 --> 00:12:11.897
"'that you are not a journalist?'

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:12.863
"Answer: 'yes'.

00:12:12.863 --> 00:12:14.237
"'So when you told your subscribers

00:12:14.237 --> 00:12:16.177
"'that you were a
journalist, you were lying?'

00:12:16.177 --> 00:12:17.740
"Answer: 'yes'."

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:20.330
And when Tasha told her
viewers that her lawyer friend

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:22.210
had reviewed Cardi's
cease and desist letter

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:24.620
and that it was bogus, she was also lying.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:25.560
Under cross examination,

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:28.070
she said that the person was
just a friend, not a lawyer.

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:30.810
This, by the way, is called
impeachment of a witness

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.150
and it can be incredibly devastating.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:33.983
She was also asked,

00:12:33.983 --> 00:12:35.697
"Isn't it true that you
lied in your deposition

00:12:35.697 --> 00:12:36.717
"when you provided a date

00:12:36.717 --> 00:12:39.170
"when you put up a video
defaming my client?"

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:40.407
Answer: "I made up a date

00:12:40.407 --> 00:12:43.260
"because you were being
combative towards me."

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:45.709
Tasha's husband kind of
threw her under the bus.

00:12:45.709 --> 00:12:48.727
Asked, "Is it true your
wife lied when she said

00:12:48.727 --> 00:12:51.440
"that there are several
businesses under Kebe Studios?"

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:52.900
Answer: "yes".

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.700
Journalist Dennis Byron,
a contributor to TMZ,

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.040
live tweeted the trial.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.400
He revealed that Tasha's husband

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.590
refuted her testimony four times.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:01.820
And then, of course, there is the evidence

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.030
about actual malice.

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:04.320
Here, the jury must've found

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.380
that Tasha K acted with actual malice.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.370
That is that she made
statements with knowledge

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.860
that it was false, or
with reckless disregard

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.518
of whether it was false or not.

00:13:12.518 --> 00:13:14.210
What evidence did the jury have

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:18.070
to show that Tasha shouldn't
have relied on Jones

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:19.610
and the other statements?

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.950
Well, Cardi's lawyers had
videos where Tasha conceded

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:26.560
that she repeated things that
she knew weren't really true.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.927
In one of the exhibits, a
phone interview, Tasha states,

00:13:28.927 --> 00:13:31.150
"Here's my thing, all of
these strippers are lying",

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:33.760
referring to Jones,
Cardi and a third party.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:36.467
In that same call, Tasha
concludes that Jones, quote,

00:13:36.467 --> 00:13:39.270
"told some truths, she
didn't tell all truths."

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:41.460
One of the most damning pieces
of evidence in this trial

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:43.300
was when the Court played a phone call

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.940
between Tasha and
celebrity blogger Lovely T,

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.990
who told Tasha that the information

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:49.440
from Starmarie Jones was fake

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:51.630
and she shouldn't repeat the claims.

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:52.670
At one point in the trial,

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:54.710
Tasha conceded that in her deposition,

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:57.680
she said it would be funny to
claim that Cardi B had HPV.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.187
Quote, "Is it a fact that you
testified in your deposition

00:14:01.187 --> 00:14:04.550
"that you thought it was
funny to say Cardi B had HPV?"

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:05.960
Answer: "yes".

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:07.148
That definitely does not put Tasha

00:14:07.148 --> 00:14:09.070
in a very sympathetic light.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:10.790
The jury also found in Cardi's favor

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:11.950
on the invasion of privacy

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.460
and intentional infliction
of emotional distress claims.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.293
In Georgia,

00:14:15.293 --> 00:14:17.290
a claim for intentional
infliction of emotional distress,

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.420
or IIED, has four elements:

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.910
that there was intentional
or reckless conduct,

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.458
which is extreme and outrageous,

00:14:23.458 --> 00:14:25.460
which caused emotional distress,

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:26.990
which is severe.

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:29.940
In support of her IIED claim,
Cardi pointed to a video

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:33.410
where Tasha says she had a
personal vendetta against Cardi.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:36.120
The jury could've found that
Tasha, therefore, had a motive

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:37.900
to defame Cardi's character.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:39.410
In this case, the jury
was probably satisfied

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:41.600
that Tasha's statements
were extreme and outrageous.

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.810
However, it's possible that
this particular verdict

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:45.137
might get overturned because,

00:14:45.137 --> 00:14:47.187
"conduct that can be
characterized as merely vulgar,

00:14:47.187 --> 00:14:48.867
"tasteless, rude or insulting

00:14:48.867 --> 00:14:51.920
"generally should not
support a claim for IIED."

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.750
Now, there was also cause of
action for invasion of privacy,

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:58.740
which, ironically, was the
name of Cardi B's debut album.

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.210
Georgia has adopted four
forms of invasion of privacy.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.700
The one at issue in this
case is invasion of privacy

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.860
through portrayal in a false light.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.980
The elements of that claim
are that the defendant

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.540
publicized a matter concerning plaintiff

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:11.540
that places plaintiff in a false light,

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.440
the defendant acts in a reckless disregard

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.100
as to the truth or falsity
of the publicized matter

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:19.188
and the false light in which
the plaintiff would be placed,

00:15:19.188 --> 00:15:21.780
and that the false light in
which the plaintiff was placed

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:23.760
would be highly offensive
to a reasonable person.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.790
And in support of her
invasion of privacy claim,

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:27.746
Cardi B emphasized the many
times that Tasha admitted

00:15:27.746 --> 00:15:30.410
that her stories were false
when she published them.

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:31.627
She apparently was quotes as saying,

00:15:31.627 --> 00:15:33.597
"You know what's funny, I make
up stories out of thin air.

00:15:33.597 --> 00:15:35.350
"Tasha just makes up stories."

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:36.737
She also said, "I knew it was fake.

00:15:36.737 --> 00:15:40.620
"I still made that stuff go viral anyway."

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:41.780
So that was probably more than enough

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:44.360
to win on that particular
invasion of privacy claim.

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.410
Now, as for the damages

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:47.930
that Cardi B is able to
recover in this case,

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:50.780
the jury awarded Cardi $1
million in general damages

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:53.340
for the reputational
damages she experienced.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:55.480
In Georgia, actual
damages explicitly include

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:58.350
impairment of reputation and
standing in the community.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.630
Cardi's complaint alleged that
some of Tasha's statements

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:04.890
were defamation per quod, and
others were defamation per se.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:07.230
Defamation per se are
statements which are considered

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.450
to be so harmful on their face

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:11.040
that the plaintiff doesn't
need to prove special damages.

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:13.990
Tasha accused Cardi of having
STIs, working as a prostitute,

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.760
committing lewd acts with a beer bottle,

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:17.340
and all of these statements likely qualify

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:20.860
as defamation per se, so Cardi
didn't have to prove damages

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:22.970
to win on liability.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.360
And many of Cardi's trial
exhibits presented proof

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:27.360
that she incurred medical expenses

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:29.360
because of emotional distress.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:31.500
Cardi B testified that
she considered suicide,

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:34.290
experienced anxiety, weight
loss, depression and migraines.

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:35.980
She also said it impacted her relationship

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:37.480
with her husband, Offset.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.990
Now, Tasha accused Cardi of having herpes,

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.196
pointing to a photograph
of a mark on her lip.

00:16:42.196 --> 00:16:44.240
People started to comment about it

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.611
on Cardi's social media posts,

00:16:45.611 --> 00:16:48.330
and when Cardi B posted a photo
of her kissing her daughter,

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.430
people commented that she was
going to give her kid herpes.

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.553
Cardi B said it had a serious
impact on her mental health

00:16:53.553 --> 00:16:55.390
and she sought treatment with a therapist

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:57.000
because of the ordeal.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.870
The therapist, Dr Sherry Blake,

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:00.720
said that during the two
years she treated Cardi,

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:01.840
her mental health deteriorated

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:03.630
because Tasha would not stop badgering her

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:05.330
with these claims.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.750
On top of that, Cardi
was awarded $1.5 million

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.260
in punitive damages.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:11.330
After the jury found Tasha
liable for defamation,

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:13.850
the lawyers offered evidence
regarding punitive damages

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.840
and attorney's fees and costs.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:17.700
Each side had 20 minutes
to present evidence,

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:20.300
but Tasha's lawyers, who are
criminal defense lawyers,

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:21.830
only took 90 seconds.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:24.700
The jury awarded Cardi an
additional $2.8 million

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:26.920
in punitive damages and attorney's fees.

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:29.920
Georgia allows punitive
damages in defamation cases

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:31.600
under certain circumstances.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:33.100
Punitive damages are given solely

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:36.220
to punish or penalize
or deter a defendant,

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.140
and to prove those damages,
the plaintiff must show

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:40.730
that the defendant's actions
showed willful misconduct,

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:43.410
malice, fraud, wantedness or oppression.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.050
If the defendant
demonstrated total disregard

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:46.230
for the consequences of her actions,

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.660
a jury can impose punitive
damages to punish that defendant.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:50.820
And a plaintiff must prove this

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:52.350
by clear and convincing evidence,

00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:54.290
which is higher than the
preponderance standard

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:56.770
that you're usually dealing
with in a civil case,

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:58.643
though there is a $250,000 cap

00:17:58.643 --> 00:18:00.670
on punitive damages in Georgia,

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:01.820
unless the plaintiff can prove

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:04.140
specific intent to cause harm.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.710
The jury deliberated for two hours

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:07.370
before deciding that Cardi B had proved

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:09.460
that Tasha intended to cause harm.

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.970
Now, there's also some really interesting

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:14.539
inside baseball here involving
Tasha K and her lawyers.

00:18:14.539 --> 00:18:17.470
Cardi B filed suit against Tasha K,

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:20.900
and Tasha K also filed
counterclaims for assault and IIED.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:24.980
So effectively, within the
same case, she sued Cardi B.

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:27.280
She asserted that Cardi
deliberately got her fans riled up

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:29.450
by falsely claiming
that Tasha was stalking

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:32.340
Cardi and her friends and
making up fake stories.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.170
She also said that Cardi called her names,

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.320
like dumb ass bitch and hoe.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.900
Tasha also said that when Cardi threatened

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:41.357
to bankrupt Tasha, by stating
quote, and I'm quoting here,

00:18:41.357 --> 00:18:42.557
"All right then bitch,

00:18:42.557 --> 00:18:44.950
"I'm gonna take all your fucking bread",

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:46.890
she meant that she was
going to get violent.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.360
Tasha said Cardi's fans
then made verbal threats,

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:50.750
and she was forced to move several times

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:51.800
because of the fans.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.170
The judge dismissed these counterclaims

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:54.943
because Tasha couldn't
prove that Cardi B herself

00:18:54.943 --> 00:18:56.240
had threatened Tasha

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:58.760
or made her believe that
she was going to harm her.

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:00.480
And although fans made lots of threats,

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:01.840
there was no evidence
that Cardi communicated

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.730
with any of these people,
let alone that she asked them

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:05.240
to take action against Tasha.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.820
And the IIED counterclaim
failed for the same reasons.

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.430
Even if Tasha suffered emotional distress

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:10.970
because Cardi's fans behaved

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:12.620
in an extreme and outrageous manner,

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:15.460
Tasha couldn't prove
causation from Cardi B.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:16.410
Since there wasn't any evidence

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:17.940
that Cardi committed these acts,

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:20.440
that she directed others to
harass and intimidate Tasha,

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:22.210
the claim was dismissed before trial.

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:23.520
And many people, including Tasha,

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:26.170
had criticism for Tasha's lawyers.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:28.230
Many news outlets concluded
that Tasha's lawyer,

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:31.120
Olga Izmaylova, was not prepared for trial

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:33.271
and had no experience
at defamation claims.

00:19:33.271 --> 00:19:35.860
Izmaylova is primarily a
criminal defense lawyer.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.240
Her cross examination of
Cardi took barely an hour,

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.910
the judge told her to
go back to law school

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:43.320
and curiously, Tasha reviewed Izmaylova

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.120
back in June of 2021,

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.730
shortly after the Court
dismissed her counterclaims.

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:49.270
According to the website AVVO,

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:52.790
which is a very mainstream
place to rate lawyers,

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:56.277
Tasha gave her lawyer one star
out of five, saying, quote,

00:19:56.277 --> 00:19:57.860
"Will not use this attorney again",

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:02.177
one star, posted by
Latasha Kebe, June 5, 2021.

00:20:02.177 --> 00:20:03.627
"Very disappointed with this attorney.

00:20:03.627 --> 00:20:05.877
"I hired her to represent
me in a defamation case,

00:20:05.877 --> 00:20:07.937
"but I will have to seek another attorney.

00:20:07.937 --> 00:20:09.727
"Olga has, on several occasions,

00:20:09.727 --> 00:20:10.867
"shown up to Court unprepared

00:20:10.867 --> 00:20:12.567
"and unfamiliar with
the facts of the case.

00:20:12.567 --> 00:20:14.737
"She advised me to file a
counter suit, which I did,

00:20:14.737 --> 00:20:17.747
"but it is clear now that
that was not the best move.

00:20:17.747 --> 00:20:19.697
"After advising me to counter sue,

